Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 58 CLINICAL DATA  Infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RADICAL MODIFIED MASTECTOMY    METASTATIC INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  PRESENT IN 1 OF 11 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  There is no residual carcinoma in the breast parenchyma  The inked surgical resection margins are negative for carcinoma    BIOPSY SITE WITH FIBROSIS  ACUTE AND CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION    FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS AND FOCAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  Diagnosis by  David Weissmann  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 19 Staff Pathologist  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of 15 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm left breast with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse and 12 x 3 x 1 5cm axillary tail  The whole specimen weighs 280 grams  A 2 6cm long  curved  healing incision is present towards one end of the specimen  5cm from nipple  3 2cm from the nearest end and 0 5cm from nearest lateral skin resection margin  Also present at the opposite end is a 3cm long  healed scar  3cm from nipple  1cm from the opposite end and 0 3cm from nearest lateral resection margin  The nipple is grossly unremarkable  Sectioning reveals a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular  firm stellate area  extending to within less than 0 1cm of the deep margin  1cm beneath the recent healing incision  No obvious biopsy cavity is identified  1cm beneath the opposite scarred area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm orange tan nodular area  1cm from the deep resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is mostly composed of unremarkable adipose tissue  except for focal white fibrous areas which contain occasional cysts  the largest less than 0 4cm  A 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm irregular stellate  white firm area is present at the proximal axillary tail  The axillary nodes range is size from REMOVED_DATE to 1cm in largest dimension and they are grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A D  entire irregular area beneath the healing incision  including overlying skin E  deep margin F  nipple G  scarred area at the other end H J  representative breast parenchyma from firmer areas K O  irregular firmer area at the proximal axillary tail and representative halves of the dissected axillary lymph nodes Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMBULATORY GEN SURGICAL   ACC 4 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST AXILLA   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 AUG 00 ACCESSIONED ON  14 AUG 00 at 15 27 CLINICAL DATA  None given                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   SEE TABLE  1   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 5cm  Grade  2 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 2cm from the inked margin of the specimen along a broad front  Stains for receptors  Requested Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 AUG 00 at 16 12                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  21 AUG 00 at 10 53 Consulting Pathologist s   Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm segment of fibroadipose tissue with accompanying radiograph film  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm well circumscribed tan gray nodule measuring approximately 0 3cm to the closest inked margin  The specimen was serially sectioned and submitted as follows  A  majority of tumor nodule with inked margin B  Remainder of nodule with accompanying inked margin C  uninvolved representative section of specimen  Resident  KENNETH HARRIS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 55 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL  95   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 1 CM   POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III  WITH EXTENSION TO INKED RESECTION MARGINS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 32     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3    SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a needle localizing needle in place  and an accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular  firm  white nodule 1 1cm in diameter  0 1cm from the inked margin  Representative section frozen as frozen section  1 and tissue saved frozen  Tissue sent for BRDU studies  The lesion is now submitted in A through D  and representative tissue in E through H  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST RIGHT BIOPSY   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Kimberly S Kirkwood  M D  Neal L Gorlick  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 51 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessels and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The The margins of the specimen appear free of tumor  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 13                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast lump is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibrofatty breast tissue  The external surface is inked in black and the specimen is sectioned to reveal an ill defined mass REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm closely present 0 4cm from the nearest inked margin  Cut surface of the mass is soft  somewhat gelatinous  multi cystic and hemorrhagic  A representative section is frozen as FX 1  now in cassette A  Representative sections in B F  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Navneet Narula  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Staff Pathologist  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  RHONDA YANTISS  M D  Jacqueline Joan Haas  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY , Unchecked.
