Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  JONATHAN M WINOGRAD  M D  Resident  Ricard Masia  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 44 year old woman with a history of IDC in left breast measuring 3 8cm by MRI  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH MILD DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  USUAL TYPE  AND DUCT ECTASIA  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  3  FOCAL PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  LCIS is present on two of eleven sections  The LCIS is located greater than 0 2cm from the inked margins of resection  An immunostain for e cadherin on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  shows focal loss of staining and supports the diagnosis  B  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH CALCIFICATIONS 2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU 3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES IN APOCRINE METAPLASIA  5  RADIAL SCAR  6  HEALING BIOPSY SITE   See table 1 and note  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 6cm  The invasive carcinoma is diffusely infiltrative with numerous small nests and trabeculae of tumor infiltrating around ducts and along fibrous stroma  Although the tumor size measurement is based on the gross examination  microscopic evaluation suggests a larger infiltrative process without an obvious discrete mass  Thus the gross measurement of 2 2cm may underestimate the true size of the tumor  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  C  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL TISSUE   EXCISION  1  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  D  SKIN  LEFT MASTECTOMY FLAP   EXCISION  SKIN AND SUB CUTIS WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED   E  SKIN  RIGHT MASTECTOMY FLAP   EXCISION  SKIN AND SUB CUTIS WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED   By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 5 containers  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a 21 x 20 x 3 5cm skin sparing simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm nipple areolar complex with a grossly unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm nipple  The specimen is oriented as follows by the surgeon  A suture indicates 12 o clock  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal fibrous breast parenchyma with areas of nodularity and multiple cysts up to 0 5cm in diameter  from which clear straw colored fluid is expressed  No focal lesions or abnormalities are identified  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the posterior portion of the specimen  including black inked posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the anterior portion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the lateral portion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the medial portion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the central portion  including areas with nodularity and cysts   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of nipple  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 3cm skin sparing simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm nipple areolar complex with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm nipple  The specimen is oriented by the surgeon as follows  Suture indicates 6 o clock  There is a surgical metal clip on the anterior surface of the specimen  in the 11 o clock position  7 5cm from the nipple areolar complex  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a firm  tan white lesion  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  located 4 8cm from the posterior margin and 2 6cm from the anterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma shows fibrocystic nodularity and cysts  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm area of firm  well demarcated yellow tissue  located 3 4cm from the posterior margin and 2 5cm from the anterior margin  and 2 5cm from the previously described lesion  The specimen is submitted as follows    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entirely submitted lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Adjacent areas of nodularity and cysts  representative sections   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area of firm yellow lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of uninvolved breast parenchyma  including posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of nipple  Received in formalin  labeled  additional left breast tissue  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  which are serially sectioned to reveal no focal lesions or abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left mastectomy flap   are 4 fragments of unremarkable tan skin with attached fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  which are serially sectioned to reveal no focal lesions or abnormalities  A representative section is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  right mastectomy flap   is a fragment of unremarkable tan skin with underlying attached fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 0 7cm  A representative section is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachu