Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 44 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm breast biopsy  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 6cm in maximum diameter white gray  well circumscribed nodule within 0 2cm of the closest inked resection margin  The specimen is submitted entirety in cassettes A through I  with nodule in A and B  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST   SUSPICIOUS NODULE  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Carlos Fernandez del castillo  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
