cent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast with axillary contents  is a 19 x 15 x 6cm left mastectomy specimen with an 11 x 9 x 2 5cm attached axillary tail  There is an overlying 16 x 8cm skin ellipse with an eccentric  unremarkable nipple areola complex  There are no evident scars on the skin surface  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm firm  stellate  tan white tumor located 0 5cm from the closest deep margin and 0 9cm from the closest anterior margin  Adjacent to this mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm rubbery area of fibrous tissue  The remaining parenchyma is interspersed with moderate amounts of dense white fibrous tissue with no additional anomalies  SECTION CODE A C  Tumor in its entirety in relation to closest deep margin  D  Lesion with adjacent fibrous area  E  Representative of unremarkable fibrous tissue from lateral aspect  F  Fibrous tissue from central aspect  G  Fibrous tissue from medial aspect  There are two ill defined  firm areas of fibrous parenchyma in the posteromedial aspect which are submitted in cassette H  Sectioning through the axillary tag reveals multiple  pink gray lymph nodes measuring up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Representative sections of each lymph node are submitted in cassettes I through K  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Arlan F Fuller Jr   M D  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
