ss with an epicenter in the upper portion of the myometrium to involve both the anterior and posterior aspects of the myometrium  This mass causes a 5 7cm exophytic protrusion into the anterior and posterior endomyometrium  The mass is very homogeneous with an only 1 0cm greatest dimension area of hemorrhage and very rare areas which are darker yellow  0 1cm in greatest dimension   Overall the mass does not display areas of softening or necrosis  There is a distinct border between the mass and the normal appearing myometrium  The mass involves almost the entire width of the myometrium and depth wise comes to within 0 4cm of the serosa in places  The boundary of the mass with the overlying endometrium is blurred with a suggestion of a 0 1cm thick endometrium overlying the mass  The exophytic portion of this mass which protrudes the endometrial cavity is  3 0cm from both the anterior and posterior lower uterine segment  The endometrium distal to the mass shows focal roughening and appears to be  0 1cm in thickness  The myometrium in the uninvolved portion of the specimen is up to 1 1cm in thickness  The mucosa of the cervix displays a tan pink herringbone like appearance and is unremarkable  The serosa of the specimen is smooth  The following sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative full cross section of the mass with its relation to the endometrium  myometrium and serosa as diagrammed   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections displaying the relationship of the mass to the overlying endometrium   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of the mass including the area of hemorrhage and the darker speckled yellow areas   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness representative section of the posterior cervix   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative full thickness section from the posterior LUS   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness representative section from the anterior cervix   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness