Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  11 MAY 98 at 17 41 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma by fine needle aspiration                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  FOCALLY FOCALLY EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INFERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  A single focus of lymphatic invasion is seen  No blood vessel or perineural invasion is seen  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for keratin will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  14 MAY 98 at 12 17                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     Immunohistochemical stains for keratin show no positive tumor cells in the sentinel lymph node on multiple levels  Added by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  15 MAY 98 at 12 47     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  A  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan red soft tissue fragment containing a 1 0cm lymph node  bisected  and submitted entirely in cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  B  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm tan yellow breast resection specimen with a long stitch marking the lateral and short stitch marking the superior border of the specimen  The specimen is entirely inked black  the superior surface is overinked blue  the anterior is overinked orange  and posterior surface is overinked green  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm in diameter tan gray firm nodule 0 2cm from the closest  inferior  soft tissue resection margin  Section code  B C  Nodule and the closest resection margin  D F  The tumor nodule submitted entirely  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   report_end  , Unchecked.
