Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 20 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast biopsy for mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  MATRIX PRODUCING METAPLASTIC TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN EXCISION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  CARCINOMA IN SITU  UNCERTAIN IF LOBULAR  OR SOLID LOW GRADE DUCTAL TYPE   SEVERAL DUCTS ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE TUMOR  WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN EXCISION MARGIN  SMALL HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  NOTE  Mucoid matrix predominates over tumor cells  which are poorly differentiated and peripherally situated  at the tumor s  leading  edge  No blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In t