esion are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   including two sections towards the nearest posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   two sections towards the area of hemorrhage in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and a section towards the overlying skin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two additional sections away from the lesion are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   including a section towards the grossly negative anterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and an additional section towards the posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The axillary tissues are dissected for lymph nodes and a number of potential lymph nodes are identified ranging in size from 0 2cm in greatest dimension to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  The potential lymph nodes are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the largest lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One potential lymph node  bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One potential lymph node  bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary tissue suggestive of the lymph node bivalved   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FORHER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has