Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 46 CLINICAL DATA  none                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 8CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO 0 2CM OF AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  microcalcifications are associated with the in situ carcinoma  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW TO INTERMEDIATE GRADE  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT IN 8 0F 9 SLIDES   EXTENDING TO 0 2CM OF SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of soft fatty tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  0 7cm  white nodule  0 3cm from the closest margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1  now A  The remainder of the nodule is in B G  Sectioning away from the nodule reveals unremarkable fatty and soft white parenchyma  Representative sections are in H and I  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
