Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 51 CLINICAL DATA  71 year old female with biopsy proven infiltrating ductal carcinoma of the left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA EXTENDING INTO THE SUPERFICIAL DERMIS IN THE REGION OF THE BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   2  ONE OF NINETEEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES WITH METASTATIC CARCINOMA  1 19  NOTE  No Paget s disease and no lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  The surgical margins are free of tumor  The positive lymph node is in the lowest third of the axilla  tumor does not extend outside of the capsule of the node  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 31                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 19 5cm  Beneath this ellipse the breast tissue is excised to a depth of 8 0cm  The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  The region of the nipple is inverted and there appears to be a 2 0cm incision in this region  Deep to this region in the breast parenchyma  there is an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area with chalky yellow mottled tissues as well as fibrosis  Grossly evident residual carcinoma is not appreciated  This region is 5 0cm from the deep margin  8 5cm from the superior margin and 6 5cm from the inferior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of fatty lobules with intervening white fibrous tissue  Focal areas of increased fibrosis and with small  0 1 to 0 2cm in diameter  blue dome cysts are identified  Multiple lymph nodes are found within the axillary tail region  the largest of which measures 2 3cm in greatest dimension and the smallest measuring 0 1cm in diameter  Section Code  A B  incision region nipple region and underlying breast tissue and old biopsy site  C E  tissue from and adjacent to the old biopsy area  F  closest deep margin  G  inferior margin and adjacent representative breast tissue  H  upper medial quadrant  representative section  I  lower medial quadrant  representative section  J  upper lateral quadrant  representative section  K  lower lateral quadrant  representative section  L Q  axillary lymph nodes  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
